        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569">

                <pb facs="0932" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg796"/>

                <head>No. 569.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                        West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 11,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 19th
                    ultimo, submitting for the consideration of this Government certain
                    correspondence on the subject of a concession granted by the Porte for the
                    erection and maintenance of thirty lights in the Red Sea, etc., and inquiring
                    whether this Government is prepared to agree to the Turkish proposals, I have
                    the honor to inform you in reply that the competent authorities of this
                    Government are not in favor of accepting the proposals in question, for the
                    reasons set forth in the inclosed copy of a report of the chairman of the
                    Light-House Board.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d569-a1.xml" xpointer="d569-a1"/>
            </div>
